Z||000033||87V6GT||08-17-2001||11:10 AM||||OK, I see the thread now. I don't usually have much time to look around much on here and didn't see it right away again at first.<BR>As a bonus for coming over and visiting with us, if you can stay around for tomm, it's the Lebanon NH Twin State car show with our own Fiero class. It's raining today, but the weather report says it should be OK tomm.<BR>I know a bunch of Pennocks regulars will be there including Cobra and Phil (the famous Hot Rod mag yellow Formula Fiero) will be there, as well as, Chester and Elvira from Newmarket. You will be able to see a bunch of us at once. <BR>We are planning on having Pizza tonight if you can join us?<BR>It would be great if you can make it to either or both.<P>Let us know on here as it looks like the whole Kelley clan is watching on it now.<P><BR>Russ Kelley<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Merrimack-RussKelley3rd.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000034||Fiero5||08-17-2001||11:19 AM||||I was trying to take two of my Fieros to the show tomm, my red 86 and my white 84. That way the Kelley's would have one Fiero from each year there. My white 84SE, my sons glow in the dark 85 GT, my red 86 SS, my Dads maroon 87GT and Marians black 88 Formula fastback.<BR>I asked Elvira who will be here at our place  in the morning (with Chester of course) for some breakfast and gorme' coffee (everyone is invited here in the morning too by the way), if she could drive one but she just had surgery is on pain meds.<BR>How about you takin' the wheel of one and driving it to the show and back for me. After the show at 3pm we all come back here for the annual Kelley Fiero cookout.<P>Let us know.<P>Steve Kelley<P>------------------<BR>                                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pegasuscolors_sig_copy.jpg">    <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||10
Z||000035||Fiero5||08-17-2001||11:39 AM||||I was just talking to Marian (Fiero2) and she reminded me that last year, Phil Randolph and Gwen came up on Friday and stayed over close to us at a hotel for the show the next day. Hey Phil, if you see this and are doing that again, you are invited to dinner tonight at our place.<BR>Pizza and fun for everyone<P><BR>Steve||||reg||6
Z||000036||Fiero2||08-17-2001||11:44 AM||||That invitation goes out to anyone who may be coming up tonight for the show tomm.<BR>Just let us know as soon as possible so we can get enough Pizza.<BR>Dinner will be around 6 to 6:30pm at our place in Plainfield NH.<P>Steve, can you give them directions?<P>Hope to see a bunch of people tonight and alot more tomm.<P>Marian<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Marians_sig_1.jpg">  <BR>I LOVE my Fiero!!!||||reg||12
Z||000037||Fiero5||08-17-2001||11:56 AM||||Sure:<P>Take I-89 North to exit 20.<BR>Coming North it's the last exit before VT -  take a left (coming south from like 93 go accross the Veterans memorial bridge from VT and exit 20 is the first exit - take a right off the ramp).<BR>You are now on Rt. 12-A. Stay straight on this road, going past McDonalds, Burger King, Pizza Hut, Wal*Mart and Price Chopper all on the left. You will pass Wendy's, Freindly's, Applebees and a Golf place (Fore-U) all on the right. Stay on this road for about 7 miles. As you come into Plainfield you will go down a steep hill. As it flattens out you will see the Library, Church, General store and Post office on the right. As you go by the Post Office (it's small so don't blink-but the sign is near the road on the right) you will go around a slight corner bending to the right. Now you will see some used cars for sale on the right (Plainfield Sales and Service). Directly on the left is a small road (Roberts road) with reflectors on metal posts on both sides at the entrance. This then turns to the right and goes dirt which becomes Spruce Park Dr. We are in the last Mobile Home on the left (yellow). Look for the Fieros.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pegasuscolors_sig_copy.jpg">    <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
Z||000038||Fiero5||08-17-2001||03:16 PM||||So where did he go?<BR>I wish Skitime would hop on a computer real soon and check his thread again.<BR>If he stops by anyones else who has seen these messages, please let him know.<P>Thanks.<P>Steve||||reg||5
Z||000039||skitime||08-17-2001||10:10 PM||||Steve - I wish we could of gotten a hold of you last night.  I stopped at a computer store in Conway this morning hoping for an answer and didn't find any. It was raining in NH this morning and we decided to get home in time to get our cars ready for the show.  We really wished we could of met you and your family as well as Chester and Elvira. Elvira I hope you are feeling better. Now that we are home I wished we were up there with the Kelleys and went to the show with them.  I hope we can meet you all sometime.  We will have to figure out a better way to communicate while on the road. Cell phones only seem to work half the time up there in the north country and it is hard to find access to a computer while on the road.  We meet a lot of great people and saw quite few cool Fieros too.  I will post Fiero pics from our trip soon. Now it is late and I have a Fiero to get ready for the show tomorrow.<P>||||reg||1
